@codelaw/rules-css-modules

The rules are reimplementations written for codelaw. Their `ported_from:` fields
name the eslint-plugin-css-modules rules (https://github.com/atfzl/eslint-plugin-css-modules,
MIT License) whose documented behaviour they reproduce; no eslint-plugin-css-modules
code or documentation text is included. `css-modules/composes-valid`, `class-naming` and
`no-global` have no source rule: they follow the CSS Modules specification
(https://github.com/css-modules/css-modules, MIT License) and the behaviour of css-loader's
`localsConvention` (https://github.com/webpack-contrib/css-loader, MIT License).
